64	// bearerTransport is an http.RoundTripper that injects the Authorization header.
65	//
66	// When token is empty, the Authorization header is omitted (rather than sent
67	// as a malformed "Authorization: Bearer "). This supports endpoints like
68	// recap that deliberately want the unauthenticated request to reach the
69	// server so it can return a typed 401 — callers that want a local fast-fail
70	// for missing auth should check ErrNotLoggedIn at construction time, not
71	// rely on the transport.
